WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:18.425
Vinnie and Mandy froze with fear.

2
00:00:19.805 --> 00:00:22.646
All the sailors stopped rowing or woke up.

3
00:00:23.906 --> 00:00:25.527
They stared at the children.

4
00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:29.668
The large man walked over to Vinnie and Mandy.

5
00:00:30.608 --> 00:00:32.690
Mandy guessed he was the captain.

6
00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:36.213
“Gunnar! Explain!

7
00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:37.634
Who are they?”

8
00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:40.176
the captain asked the fair boy.

9
00:00:40.196 --> 00:00:44.239
“Sir, I don’t know,” the boy replied.

10
00:00:44.259 --> 00:00:46.381
“Why did you hide here?

11
00:00:47.001 --> 00:00:49.243
Do you want to be warriors like Gunnar?”

12
00:00:50.444 --> 00:00:53.407
The captain pointed his sword at Vinnie and Mandy.

13
00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:55.628
“Yes, sir!”

14
00:00:56.229 --> 00:00:57.050
Vinnie shouted.

15
00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:59.832
“Ah, true Viking spirit!”

16
00:01:00.632 --> 00:01:01.613
the captain said.

17
00:01:01.633 --> 00:01:04.335
“I like your courage, boy.”

18
00:01:05.496 --> 00:01:08.419
The captain slapped Vinnie on the back.

19
00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.941
Vinnie nearly fell over.

20
00:01:12.763 --> 00:01:15.225
The captain stopped and glared at Mandy.

21
00:01:15.245 --> 00:01:16.786
“But you!

22
00:01:17.647 --> 00:01:20.490
Little girls should not be sneaking onto a Viking ship.

23
00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.193
Especially one as weak as you,” he sneered.

24
00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:27.656
Mandy threw back her head proudly.

25
00:01:28.704 --> 00:01:33.665
“I may look weak, sir,” she replied in a clear, loud voice.

26
00:01:33.685 --> 00:01:36.606
“But I am as strong as a horse.”

27
00:01:36.626 --> 00:01:39.387
“Land ho!”

28
00:01:40.107 --> 00:01:41.188
the lookout shouted.

29
00:01:41.208 --> 00:01:44.088
“Finally!” the captain said.

30
00:01:44.108 --> 00:01:46.369
“Get ready to go ashore.”

31
00:01:47.389 --> 00:01:52.251
Turning to Vinnie and Mandy, he said, “You two—stay with Gunnar.”

32
00:01:54.851 --> 00:01:58.817
Mandy let out a sigh of relief as the captain turned away.

33
00:01:58.837 --> 00:02:04.859
“Vinnie! I don’t think he likes me being on the ship,” she said.

34
00:02:04.879 --> 00:02:06.200
“Don’t worry.

35
00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.681
You were really brave,” Vinnie replied.

36
00:02:10.482 --> 00:02:11.742
He turned to Gunnar.

37
00:02:11.762 --> 00:02:13.483
“Where are we going?”

38
00:02:13.923 --> 00:02:14.504
he asked.

39
00:02:14.524 --> 00:02:18.065
“This port is Kaupang.

40
00:02:19.066 --> 00:02:24.488
It is a Viking village where we trade and sell our goods,” Gunnar said proudly.

41
00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:27.425
“The captain is the best bear hunter!

42
00:02:28.505 --> 00:02:31.686
He brought bear skins from our village in the icy North.”

43
00:02:31.706 --> 00:02:34.027
“Here we go, Vinnie.

44
00:02:34.447 --> 00:02:37.048
Look!” Mandy grabbed his arm.

45
00:02:39.609 --> 00:02:42.709
The Sleeping Dragon pulled smoothly into port.

46
00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:47.251
Several other Viking ships were already docked there.

47
00:02:48.671 --> 00:02:50.632
Each ship was long and slender.

48
00:02:51.568 --> 00:02:55.370
Viking sailors carried large chests out of the ships.

49
00:02:56.811 --> 00:02:59.312
Some carried smaller boxes of jewelry.

50
00:02:59.332 --> 00:03:03.655
“Gunnar!” the captain called out.

51
00:03:03.675 --> 00:03:07.497
“Take this to Old Dirk, the blacksmith.”

52
00:03:08.777 --> 00:03:11.539
The captain handed Gunnar a jewelry box.

53
00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.220
“Tell him I sent you.

54
00:03:15.141 --> 00:03:16.301
He will know what to do.”

55
00:03:16.321 --> 00:03:21.064
“Yes, captain,” said Gunnar as he took the box.

56
00:03:22.208 --> 00:03:25.671
“Do not disappoint me,” the captain roared.

57
00:03:25.691 --> 00:03:28.252
“And keep an eye on those two.”

58
00:03:29.453 --> 00:03:31.354
He pointed to Vinnie and Mandy.

59
00:03:31.374 --> 00:03:32.655
“Come on!”

60
00:03:33.196 --> 00:03:34.096
Gunnar called.

61
00:03:35.457 --> 00:03:38.760
Vinnie and Mandy followed him off the Sleeping Dragon.

62
00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.562
Kaupang was a busy open market.

63
00:03:43.783 --> 00:03:46.665
People exchanged furs for iron weapons.

64
00:03:47.766 --> 00:03:53.338
Others bought bear skins, walrus tusks, and whale bones with silver coins.

65
00:03:54.999 --> 00:03:58.882
Finally the children arrived at the blacksmith’s workshop.

66
00:04:00.303 --> 00:04:02.945
The boy introduced himself to the blacksmith.

67
00:04:02.965 --> 00:04:04.747
“I am Gunnar.

68
00:04:05.287 --> 00:04:07.109
Captain Skull-Crusher sent me.”

69
00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:10.972
Vinnie and Mandy stared at each other.

70
00:04:10.992 --> 00:04:15.495
“Skull-Crusher?” they gasped.
